    "problem_statement": "Job cancellation not working properly - jobs remain in scheduler after cancel_job\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen calling `cancel_job()` on a scheduled job, the job is not being properly removed from the scheduler. Instead of being removed, the job appears to be added back to the jobs list, causing the scheduler to retain jobs that should have been cancelled.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport schedule\n\ndef my_job():\n    print(\"Job executed\")\n\n# Schedule a job\njob = schedule.every().second.do(my_job)\nprint(f\"Jobs before cancel: {len(schedule.jobs)}\")  # Should be 1\n\n# Try to cancel the job\nschedule.cancel_job(job)\nprint(f\"Jobs after cancel: {len(schedule.jobs)}\")   # Should be 0, but shows 1\n\n# The job is still there and will continue to run\nschedule.run_pending()\n```\n\nAlso affects jobs that return `CancelJob`:\n\n```python\nimport schedule\n\ndef stop_job():\n    return schedule.CancelJob\n\nschedule.every().second.do(stop_job)\nschedule.every().second.do(stop_job) \nschedule.every().second.do(stop_job)\nprint(f\"Jobs scheduled: {len(schedule.jobs)}\")  # Shows 3\n\nschedule.run_all()  # Should cancel all jobs\nprint(f\"Jobs remaining: {len(schedule.jobs)}\")  # Should be 0, but shows 3\n```\n\nThe `until()` functionality is also broken - jobs that should expire and be removed automatically are not being cleaned up properly."
